    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2EyFt56QD749nzNEM2sdoDc)_\n\n**Before:** many module docs describe a function or a change in one long paragraph of four or five sentences, which is slow to scan.\n\n**After:** the prose in `docs/tangles/**` and `docs/architecture/` and `docs/main.org` is broken into a one-line lead plus short bullets, grouped by what each bullet says (what it does, dependencies, caveats, known bugs, status).\n- About 140 docs changed, roughly 700 paragraphs. Every paragraph over 200 characters with two or more sentences was rewritten.\n- The repeated \"Literate source for ...\" intro is now three bullets (what is in the blocks, where `:tangle` is set, link to the README).\n- Wording is kept; no facts were added or removed. Known bugs and \"not tested\" notes are still there, now as lists.\n- Left as written on purpose: text quoted from other manuals or posts (`org-config`, `denote`, `dashboard`, `search`, `file-management`, `sp-typesetting`, `sp-helper-functions`), and a few personal notes (`reading`, `dms`, `task`, `sp-appearance-overview`, part of `zettelkasten`). Say if you want those done as well.\n\n**Checked:** for all 179 `.org` docs, the contents of every source block, every `#+begin`/`#+end` line, `#+PROPERTY` lines and `:tangle`/`:header-args` property lines are byte-identical to `main` (script compared before and after), so the tangled `.el` files do not change. Rebased on current `main`. **Not checked:** I did not run `org-babel-tangle` (no Emacs in the container), and did not render the docs in Org, so list spacing is only checked by reading the diff.\n\nCHANGELOG.org is not touched (docs only, as requested).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01DYckdVfiNhwhqVYDRKGLKX)_",
    "changed_files": 142,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-24T19:30:25Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `build` check fails, but not because of this PR. `architecture/load-order.org` on `main` still has unresolved merge-conflict markers (`<<<<<<< HEAD` / `=======` / `>>>>>>> main` at lines 57–73, 160–164 and 201–205). Inside the dot block they make Graphviz fail with `syntax error in line 60 near '>'`. This PR only touches one prose paragraph in that file (bulleted \"How to read the boxes and arrows\"), so it keeps the markers as they are.\n\nI'm not resolving them here because picking which side of each conflict is correct belongs to whoever merged the load-order changes (likely the ADR 0009 reorder), and it would mix an unrelated fix into a docs-style PR. Once `main` is fixed, this PR should go green after a rebase or \"Update branch\".\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
